{{/*
  Custom values table. Differs from the built-in `chart.valuesSection` in two ways,
  both to keep the rendered table inside the 800px article column on the Octopus
  docs site (https://octopus.com/docs/argo-cd/instances):

    1. No `Type` column - the `Default` cell already shows `""` / `[]` / `{}` /
       `true` / `1`, which tells you the type.
    2. Parent-object rows are dropped when their children are documented
       individually, so we don't render an unbreakable JSON blob (e.g.
       `gateway.serviceAccount`) immediately above rows that repeat it.
       The check scans `$.Values` (every row in the chart), not just the current
       section, because a parent and its children can land in different sections.

  Corollary for values.yaml: never leave a whole object as the only documented
  row. Annotate each leaf under it with `# --` instead, and the parent row
  disappears on its own while every value gets a row of its own.

  Section headings are sentence case, per Octopus house style. Named sections
  come verbatim from the `@section` annotation in values.yaml; the catch-all
  heading is hardcoded below because helm-docs' own default is "Other Values".
*/}}
